        "original_id": "694e323c-c9ac-5428-82b7-2e883008a3df",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sutera, Province of Caltanissetta, Sicily, Palermo, Caltanissetta\n- Plants: Rhodotypos scandens, Rhodotypos, Kerria\n- Organizations: Rosaceae\n\nFacts:\n- Sutera is a comune, or municipality, in the Province of Caltanissetta in the Italian region of Sicily.\n- Sutera is located about 70 km southeast of Palermo and about 30 km west of Caltanissetta.\n- Rhodotypos scandens is the only species in the genus Rhodotypos.\n- Rhodotypos scandens is a deciduous shrub in the family Rosaceae.\n- Some botanists consider Rhodotypos scandens closely related to Kerria and include it in the genus Kerria.",
